1494	  /* A progress bar that emits light rather than just being filled in. */
1495	  /* The glow on `.bar-fill` never reached the concept's bloom because
1496	     `.bar-track` needs `overflow: hidden` to clip the fill to its actual
1497	     WIDTH (a percentage bar), and that same clip cuts off any box-shadow
1498	     glow on what it contains — a shadow cannot escape its own clipping
1499	     ancestor. `.glow-bar` is the fix: an unclipped copy of the fill, same
1500	     width, sitting behind the track and blurred, so the bloom can spread
1501	     past the track's own box the way the reference does. The track keeps a
1502	     smaller inset glow of its own for a lit edge close up. */
1503	  .bar-track { position: relative; background: rgba(6, 16, 38, 0.66); box-shadow: inset 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); }
1504	  .bar-fill  { position: relative; box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(210, 245, 255, 0.65), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.35); }
1505	  .glow-bar  { filter: blur(7px); opacity: 0.9; pointer-events: none; }
